|17|45||bib14|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10205316</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Duthie</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Folic acid deficiency and cancer: mechanisms of DNA instability</article-title><source>Br Med Bull</source><year>1999</year><volume>55</volume><supplement>3</supplement><fpage>578</fpage><lpage>592</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Br Med Bull||55|578||bib15|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10746348</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Duthie</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Grant</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Narayanan</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Increased uracil misincorporation in lymphocytes from folate-deficient rats</article-title><source>Br J Cancer</source><year>2000a</year><volume>83</volume><fpage>1532</fpage><lpage>1537</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Br J Cancer||83|1532||bib16|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11076664</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Duthie</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hawdon</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>DNA instability (strand breakage, uracil misincorporation, and defective repair) is increased by folic acid depletion in human lymphocytes <italic>in vitro</italic></article-title><source>FASEB</source><year>1998</year><volume>12</volume><supplement>4</supplement><fpage>1491</fpage><lpage>1497</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'FASEB||12|1491||bib17|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Duthie</surname><given-names>SJ</given